  "conclusions": [
    "The physical card advertises MMC 5.1, HS200/HS400 at 1.8V; current HS_TIMING remains legacy.",
    "The same controller and card family previously ran 8-bit HS400 at 200MHz in the BSP; this is real-board capability evidence, not current driver acceptance.",
    "Effective BSP FDT routes VCCQ to AXP8191 ALDO3; saved regulator state reads 1800mV and IOS reports 1.8V. VCC and VCCQ are distinct.",
    "Current mainline fixed pc-1v8-firmware describes inherited pad supply; IOS 3.3V alone does not establish physical VCCQ. Do not change PMIC voltage based on that default.",
    "Implement and validate DMA at unchanged 12MHz/8-bit/legacy first. Higher modes require host clock/timing, card transitions, tuning, DS handling and fallback checks; capability flags alone are insufficient.",
    "Enhanced strobe card support is not proof of implemented enhanced-strobe host operation."
  ],
  "current_high_speed_acceptance": false,
  "recommendation": "Preserve existing 1.8V VCCQ/pin settings; stage DMA, HS52, HS200 tuning, then HS400 with actual controller and card evidence."
